# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# ONE value is required. Everything below it is for self-hosting the push path, and most people
# should leave all of it commented out.

# Your Bambuddy API key. Trellis polls Bambuddy with it, and validates the key the APP presents
# against Bambuddy too, so the same key works for both.
#   printf 'BAMBUDDY_API_KEY=%s\n' "$(tr -d '[:space:]' < <secrets-dir>/bb_apikey)" >> .env
BAMBUDDY_API_KEY=


# ─── push: leave this whole section alone unless you are self-hosting ───────────────────────────
#
# With nothing set here, Trellis relays through the push service run by the app's author. That is
# the default and it needs no Apple developer account, no APNs key, and no push certificate.
# Trellis enrols itself on first start and prints a RECOVERY CODE once, to the log — save it, it is
# the only way to re-adopt your bindings if data/tenant.json is lost.
#
# Want your own push service? Run your own Canopy — it is where every Apple credential belongs, and
# Trellis holds none of them either way. It needs your own Apple team AND your own BUILD of the app,
# because APNs keys are team-scoped and the topic is the bundle id: docs/guides/self-hosting-push.md

# Point at your own Canopy instead of the author's.
#CANOPY_URL=https://canopy.example.com

# Some relays gate enrolment while they are young. Without it a gated relay answers 403 and push
# stays off; Trellis logs this variable by name when that happens.
#CANOPY_INVITE_CODE=

# ─── MakerWorld collections (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Bambuddy's docker volume, mounted read-only so the collection endpoints can read the stored Bambu
# Cloud token — that token stays on your server rather than going to a phone. The default is the
# name compose generates for deploy/bambuddy/; check yours with:
#   docker inspect bambuddy --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{.Name}}{{end}}'
# Compose refuses to start on a wrong name, so this is loud rather than silent.
#BAMBUDDY_VOLUME=bambuddy_bambuddy_data
